    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "86595da1-507b-32f2-af9b-85575febf003",
                "word": "um",
                "pos": "intj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1e55afc7-a11f-388a-a2a3-5797727b36ac",
                        "entry_id": "86595da1-507b-32f2-af9b-85575febf003",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Expression of hesitation, uncertainty or space filler in conversation."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c558f584-ebe1-44de-9b8b-b479f9d71049",
                                "sense_id": "1e55afc7-a11f-388a-a2a3-5797727b36ac",
                                "text": "Um, I don’t know."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ab2470c1-286f-4e7a-b84b-06be0047ee5f",
                                "sense_id": "1e55afc7-a11f-388a-a2a3-5797727b36ac",
                                "text": "Let’s see... um... how about this?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d9442994-a9fa-492d-b585-975d48219255",
                                "sense_id": "1e55afc7-a11f-388a-a2a3-5797727b36ac",
                                "text": "It's a great test of the claims of open-source gurus, who say that a self-motivated community can outcode any team working for a single employer—like, um, Microsoft."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6bbad0a0-2130-4e34-8bce-cf83e9735b64",
                                "sense_id": "1e55afc7-a11f-388a-a2a3-5797727b36ac",
                                "text": "As the years go by, speech reverts to childhood levels of disfluency, with more pauses, more errors, more repeated words, but even the peak years are not great: up to 8 percent of the average person’s word output consists of meaningless fillers and placeholders like um, uh and er."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5aae1e29-043f-48d9-991b-43951afa28c4",
                                "sense_id": "1e55afc7-a11f-388a-a2a3-5797727b36ac",
                                "text": "Um And I don't know um what to say to the court other than, I don't know how we could get through 1/5 of that."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ec6a18aa-58f6-3dfd-a0a5-e10d3813975c",
                        "entry_id": "86595da1-507b-32f2-af9b-85575febf003",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Dated spelling of mmm."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "US"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "39b2b066-42fd-4c06-97b2-e4c1e6d4df95",
                                "sense_id": "ec6a18aa-58f6-3dfd-a0a5-e10d3813975c",
                                "text": "\"About the same, wherever you go,\" he agreed.\n\"Um,\" I said."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "71700d1b-5ecf-38a5-b5fa-67c5d2a77132",
                        "entry_id": "86595da1-507b-32f2-af9b-85575febf003",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An expression to forcefully call attention to something wrong."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "959f9fe5-98f5-44a2-bbeb-64f5cab39560",
                                "sense_id": "71700d1b-5ecf-38a5-b5fa-67c5d2a77132",
                                "text": "Um, excuse me!"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a4a41a7b-aff6-3b0f-b309-435dde08950e",
                        "entry_id": "86595da1-507b-32f2-af9b-85575febf003",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An expression of shocked disapproval used by a child who witnesses forbidden behavior."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "childish"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9b5ee012-a95d-4b4f-8602-a5a2eb7b9aeb",
                                "sense_id": "a4a41a7b-aff6-3b0f-b309-435dde08950e",
                                "text": "While I was in her room, Sam walked by and said, “Um, I'm telling!”\n“You're telling what?” I asked.\n“You're reading Tori's journal,” she said."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a0da11f8-c0d9-4eac-aaf1-8c0f9bc1865b",
                                "sense_id": "a4a41a7b-aff6-3b0f-b309-435dde08950e",
                                "text": "Mair used to look after Laura. If anyone threatened to tease her, Mair would stand up straight, point her finger at the enemy and shout, 'Um! I'm telling on you!'"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
